<section class="shell architecture" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
  <div class="heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Current architecture</p>
      <h2 id="architecture-title">Independent cores. Typed boundaries. One composition.</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="muted explanation">
      The voice model is the realtime interaction layer. M.A.R.K. remains the platform around it,
      including lifecycle, tools, intelligence, memory, and state.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="diagram" role="img" aria-label="User microphone flows through the AEC boundary and Realtime Core to Gemini Live. Assistant Runtime connects independent Tool, Intelligence, Memory, and State cores through typed adapters.">
    <div class="live-label eyebrow">Native speech path</div>
    <div class="live-path">
      <div class="node external"><span class="mono">01</span><strong>User / microphone</strong><small>capture</small></div>
      <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div class="node boundary"><span class="mono">02</span><strong>AEC boundary</strong><small>signal relationship · needs work</small></div>
      <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div class="node core"><span class="mono">03</span><strong>Realtime Core</strong><small>session boundary</small></div>
      <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div class="node provider"><span class="mono">04</span><strong>Gemini Live</strong><small>voice interaction</small></div>
    </div>

    <div class="adapter-line" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><b>typed adapters</b><span></span></div>

    <div class="composition">
      <div class="composition-label">
        <span class="eyebrow">Composition root</span>
        <strong>assistant-runtime</strong>
        <small>owns lifecycle, correlation, cancellation, and delivery</small>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="branches" aria-label="Independent boundaries">
      <div class="branch"><strong>direct response</strong><small>Realtime Core → voice model</small></div>
      <div class="branch"><strong>Tool System</strong><small>bounded execution and policy</small></div>
      <div class="branch"><strong>Intelligence Core</strong><small>async delegation and reasoning</small></div>
      <div class="branch"><strong>Memory / State Core</strong><small>owned by their own boundaries</small></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="note tiny">
    Cores remain independent repositories with zero direct imports between them. The AEC node is an
    explicit boundary under work, not a claim that Mark II is already full-duplex.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .architecture{padding-top:40px}
  .heading{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr minmax(260px,34ch);gap:32px;align-items:end}
